# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule 7.4 on the esp-hosted port's ThreadX object-name buffers.
# ThreadX takes object names as `CHAR*`, not `const CHAR*`, so the port gives
# each name its own writable array -- `static char s_tx_name_eh_edge[] =
# "eh_edge";` -- rather than casting a literal and dropping a qualifier the
# object really has (which is what `-Wcast-qual -Werror` correctly rejects).
# Rule 7.4 forbids ASSIGNING a string literal to an object that is not a
# pointer to const-qualified char. Initialising a char ARRAY from a literal is
# a copy, not an assignment of the literal's address, and is explicitly outside
# the rule -- the array is the object, and nothing aliases the literal. cppcheck
# does not draw that distinction here (and inconsistently: it charges only one
# of the port's three identical name buffers), so this is a tooling gap, not a
# deviation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
